      ["After a strong move, price usually pulls back before continuing. <b>Fibonacci retracement</b> levels (23.6%, 38.2%, 50%, 61.8%, 78.6%) mark common pullback depths.",
       "Draw from the swing low to the swing high in an uptrend (high to low in a downtrend). When a Fibonacci level, a previous support and a bullish candle all line up, you have a high-quality entry. Extensions (127.2%, 161.8%) suggest targets."],
