course('structure', 'Price action and market structure', 'fa-sitemap',
       'Structure, break of structure, change of character, order blocks, fair value gaps, liquidity, supply and demand.', [
    t('market-structure', 'Market structure: HH, HL, LH, LL', ['Bullish structure: higher highs + higher lows.', 'Bearish structure: lower highs + lower lows.',
                                                               'Structure tells you which side to trade.'],
      ["Price moves in swings. Label each swing high and low: <b>HH/HL</b> means buyers are in control, <b>LH/LL</b> means sellers are. As long as the structure holds, look for trades in its direction.",
       "In an uptrend the last <b>higher low</b> is the key level: if it breaks, the uptrend is in doubt."], pic='uptrend'),
    t('bos', 'Break of structure (BOS)', ['Price closes beyond the previous swing in the trend direction.', 'Confirms the trend continues.'],
      ["A <b>break of structure</b> happens when price closes above the last higher high in an uptrend (or below the last lower low in a downtrend). It confirms the trend is still alive.",
       "After a BOS, traders wait for a pullback to a demand zone, order block or Fibonacci level to join the trend."], pic='bos'),
    t('choch', 'Change of character (CHoCH)', ['The first break against the trend.', 'In a downtrend: price breaks the last lower high.',
                                               'Early sign of a reversal; wait for a pullback.'],
      ["A <b>change of character</b> is the first time price breaks structure <b>against</b> the trend: in a downtrend, a close above the last lower high. It says sellers have lost control.",
       "CHoCH is an early signal; the safer entry is the pullback that forms a higher low afterwards."], pic='choch'),
    t('order-blocks', 'Order blocks', ['The last opposite candle before a strong move.', 'Where big orders were placed; price often returns there.',
                                       'Bullish OB: last red candle before a strong rally.'],
      ["An <b>order block</b> is the last bearish candle before a strong bullish move (bullish OB), or the last bullish candle before a strong drop (bearish OB). Institutions likely built positions there.",
       "When price returns to that zone, it often reacts. Combine it with structure: a bullish OB that caused a break of structure is far stronger."], pic='order_block'),
    t('fvg', 'Fair value gaps (imbalance)', ['A 3-candle gap: candle 1\'s high doesn\'t overlap candle 3\'s low.', 'Price often comes back to fill part of it.'],
      ["A <b>fair value gap</b> appears when a big candle moves so fast that the wicks of the candles on either side do not overlap. The market left an imbalance.",
       "Price frequently retraces into the gap before continuing. A bullish FVG in an uptrend is a pullback entry zone."], pic='fvg'),
    t('liquidity', 'Liquidity and stop hunts', ['Stops cluster above equal highs and below equal lows.', 'Price often sweeps them before reversing.',
                                                'Don\'t put your stop exactly at the obvious level.'],
      ["Many traders put stops just below obvious lows or above obvious highs. These clusters are <b>liquidity</b>: big players need it to fill large orders.",
       "A <b>liquidity sweep</b> is a quick move beyond the level that closes back inside: stops are triggered, then price reverses. A sweep followed by a bullish engulfing is a classic setup. Give your own stop a little extra room beyond obvious levels."],
      pic='liquidity_sweep'),
    t('supply-demand', 'Supply and demand zones', ['Demand: a base before a strong rally.', 'Supply: a base before a strong drop.',
                                                   'Fresh (untested) zones work best.'],
      ["A <b>demand zone</b> is the small consolidation right before a strong rally; a <b>supply zone</b> the base before a strong drop. Unfilled orders often remain there.",
       "The first return to a fresh zone has the best odds. Each later test weakens it."], pic='supply_demand'),
    t('price-action-entry', 'Building a price action entry', ['1. Higher-timeframe direction.', '2. A key zone.', '3. A trigger candle.', '4. Stop beyond the zone.', '5. Target the next level.'],
      ["Put the pieces together: (1) the 4H/daily structure says up; (2) price pulls back into a demand zone or order block that lines up with support; (3) on the 15m/1H a bullish engulfing or hammer forms; (4) the stop goes below the zone; (5) the target is the previous high, giving at least 1:2.",
       "Write the plan before you click. If any piece is missing, skip the trade."]),
])

